From 9c11a9553df2f42848bd605cefe892049db418d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 17:30:00 -0800
Subject: defaultenv: mnt-pocket-reform-radxa-cm5: add disp-reset init script

Send the 'r' SPI command to the RP2040 system controller at barebox
startup to pulse the panel hardware RESX line (PIN_DISP_RESET, GPIO 2)
before autoboot.

The RP2040 pulses RESX on cold boot but not on warm reboot. Without this
pulse, the Wisecoco V2 panel (ER88477) gets a blank screen because DSI
init races against an uninitialized panel. The JDI V1 panel may also
benefit from a clean reset on warm reboot.

The reform2_lpc protocol (matching the Linux reform2_lpc.c driver) requires
two separate SPI transactions with a 50ms gap between them: one to write
the command, one to read the response. The RP2040 processes the command in
a timer interrupt after the first transaction's CS deasserts, then fills
its TX FIFO before the second transaction clocks out the response. Skipping
the read transaction, or combining write and read into one transaction,
gives the RP2040 no time to respond and the read (if attempted at all)
comes back all zeros.

Command bytes: { 0xb5, 0x72, 0x01, 0xc6 }
  0xb5 = LPC magic, 0x72 = 'r' (display reset), 0x01 = trigger,
  0xc6 = XOR checksum. Response is 8 bytes (ignored); RESX pulse occurs
  after the response is sent, so the trailing 50ms after each transaction
  covers both the 20ms pulse and panel stabilization time.

This script hardcodes bus 0, matching this board's own spi_lpc alias
(patch 0004). That's only meaningful for boards that actually have this
node - the RCORE-based boards sharing reform2_rk3588_probe() do not.
Originally landed in defaultenv-mnt-reform2-rk3588, the directory shared
by every board using that probe function, meaning it would have run
unconditionally on RCORE boards too, where bus 0 is not this board's
RP2040 but potentially any Rockchip SPI controller depending on probe
order (see patch 0006's commit message for the bus-numbering bug this
depends on). Moved to a new board-specific defaultenv-mnt-pocket-reform-
radxa-cm5 directory, gated behind a new has_disp_reset_env field on
struct reform2_model, set only for this board, so this script cannot
run - and cannot address whatever ends up on bus 0 - on any board
except this one.

Depends on: RP2040 firmware with 'r' command support
            spi-gpio node in DTS (patch 0004)

Signed-off-by: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
